{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code","id":1126808,"title":"[Open Dev] The Code","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-09T12:38:52-07:00","id":1126808,"title":"[Open Dev] The Code","content":"Huh. Guess I'll do one of these things.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revisiting-the-code-hunter-the-vigil/\" target=\"_blank\">Anyways, new open dev blog</a>. This time covering the hunter Code.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T13:29:21-07:00","id":1126824,"title":"","content":"Exposing someone else to the Supernatural is a 10-7 breaking point? That's going to be rough on Network Zero players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T13:31:03-07:00","id":1126825,"title":"","content":"One problem:<br /> <br /> Why is mind control a <i>penalty?</i><br /> <br /> Besides being very likely to piss a player off for no good reason, it doesn't make sense in the context of the Code (&quot;That literally was not me. I am not like that-that is what makes me different&quot;).<br /> <br /> Otherwise, this looks awesome! I love the &quot;success&quot; Conditions, showing that psychologically, a hunter <i>really is </i>a bit different from everyone else, dealing with psychological strain by drowning it in work. It's easy to see the slasher that lurks at the heart of a hunter, and it is freaking beautiful.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, I think the Secret Frequency's Code is different from the basic one-that's probably replaced with &quot;Not exposing the supernatural elements behind another person's breaking point to that person.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 08-09-2017, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T13:41:05-07:00","id":1126829,"title":"","content":"Yeah I wouldn't be surprised in the splat write ups for each Compact and Conspiracy, they have their own Code additions/revisions that are exclusive to those factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T13:52:52-07:00","id":1126833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1126825#post1126825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem:<br /> <br /> Why is mind control a <i>penalty?</i><br /> <br /> Besides being very likely to piss a player off for no good reason, it doesn't make sense in the context of the Code (&quot;That literally was not me. I am not like that-that is what makes me different&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps because the removal of your free will in the matter is extra traumatic? Hunters still function off of Integrity, for the most part, and Integrity is all about things your character finds traumatic.<br /> <br /> That being said, how does everyone else feel about there being &quot;levels&quot; of Integrity Breaking Points? It looks quite similar to Wisdom in that regard, and it seems to touch on Humanity with the way that lower Integrity means being less impacted by Breaking Points. It feels like a way to add mechanics to Breaking Points no longer impacting you, but I'm not sure I like the implications of people with lower Integrity being increasingly violent and more resistant to trauma when the CofD core presents low-Integrity characters as <i>more </i>likely to suffer from and fail Breaking Points, not less. I don't know, maybe this is just a matter of presentation or the warped perspective of Hunters, but it feels very 1E in that regard and has unfortunate implications regarding people who have experienced trauma.<br /> <br /> It also feels a little bit... off... that Hunters get Touchstones when regular mortals and even Mages (who are, for the most part, human) do not. That's easily fixed with house rules, though, so it's kind of a non-issue.<br /> <br /> I <i>do </i>like that there's the twist of being able to build Integrity (and be better at handling Breaking Points) if you open up to someone or make an act of self-sacrifice. That is something that I really enjoy and would like to see incorporated some more, because that builds off of Touchstones in a delicious way that reminds me of Atrocity from Danse Macabre without all the gross bits where opening up to the people who matter to you puts strain on the relationship and pushes them away.<br /> <br /> One thing that I find really strange though is that &quot;Inflicting Serious Harm to a Person&quot; is an Integrity 10-7 Breaking Point and a Code Breaking Point too? So, what, your average PC loses a dot of Integrity and then all of a sudden they're cool with brutalizing or murdering people but not with torturing them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T13:53:57-07:00","id":1126834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1126825#post1126825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem:<br /> <br /> Why is mind control a <i>penalty?</i><br /> <br /> Besides being very likely to piss a player off for no good reason, it doesn't make sense in the context of the Code (&quot;That literally was not me. I am not like that-that is what makes me different&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Integrity is not just about violating the Code, it's about one's confidence being shaken. And breaking the code under mind control can be a confidence-shaking experience. Someone or something out there can make you break the code, no matter how you feel about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1126824#post1126824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exposing someone else to the Supernatural is a 10-7 breaking point? That's going to be rough on Network Zero players.</div> </div> </div> </div>People rarely stay above 7 in these games. You start with 7. If you want more, Network Zero, a group that is devoted to turning the world as everyone knows it entirely upside down, is probably not the way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T14:02:19-07:00","id":1126838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1126833#post1126833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps because the removal of your free will in the matter is extra traumatic? Hunters still function off of Integrity, for the most part, and Integrity is all about things your character finds traumatic.<br /> <br /> That being said, how does everyone else feel about there being &amp;quot;levels&amp;quot; of Integrity Breaking Points? It looks quite similar to Wisdom in that regard, and it seems to touch on Humanity with the way that lower Integrity means being less impacted by Breaking Points. It feels like a way to add mechanics to Breaking Points no longer impacting you, but I'm not sure I like the implications of people with lower Integrity being increasingly violent and more resistant to trauma when the CofD core presents low-Integrity characters as <i>more </i>likely to suffer from and fail Breaking Points, not less. I don't know, maybe this is just a matter of presentation or the warped perspective of Hunters, but it feels very 1E in that regard and has unfortunate implications regarding people who have experienced trauma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters do questionable hard things. Asks a soldier if killing can get easier or harder the more trauma you experience. The assumption is that they become more callous to dealing with the loss of their friends, expecting it to happen again. Also much of the trauma is self inflicted by the things they choose to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T14:04:00-07:00","id":1126841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1126825#post1126825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem:<br /> <br /> Why is mind control a <i>penalty?</i><br /> <br /> Besides being very likely to piss a player off for no good reason, it doesn't make sense in the context of the Code (&quot;That literally was not me. I am not like that-that is what makes me different&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's specifically at the discretion of the ST, and not everyone minds that kind of thing. Also...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whenever a hunter character violates the Code or <b>experiences something that drastically shakes his confidence</b>, </div> </div> </div>Being mind contolled seems exactly like it'd be more likely to make a hunter double-down on the paranoid Vigil life-style that lower integrity seems to represent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T14:35:38-07:00","id":1126850,"title":"","content":"Is it my reading, or does hunters Integrity is shaken only on first killing particular monster? 'Oh, I killed one vampire, now I can kill thousands!' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe next kills should be move to higher 'tier' of Integrity sins, to borrow Mage 2E terminology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T14:35:40-07:00","id":1126851,"title":"","content":"There's something I find hard to reconcile in my head. &quot;Integrity&quot; states that characters on its lower end become more ruthless and obsessive. However, &quot;Breaking Points&quot; shows that losing Integrity makes characters insecure and filled with doubt. Perhaps I'm missing something, but it seems these rules incorporate clashing ideas.<br /> <br /> They also show that going through a Breaking Point results in loss of confidence on one end, or radicalization on another. None of these offer clarity or regained sense of perspective. That could very well be intended, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T14:50:39-07:00","id":1126854,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing the obsessiveness is a reaction to insecurity. One cannot be sure of the world, so one clings to one thing. Plus a result of all those Conditions you get from the Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Like John's lost 4 Integrity. 3 of those Breaking Points were while he was being mind controlled. He can come out of that with a sureness that all mind controllers absolutely must be killed. And, because he's evidence of it, anyone who shows susceptibility to mind control cannot be trusted at all and are better off dead than a potential threat to him or living a tormented life dreading the things they've done under the control of monsters. He's of course able to not count himself among that group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-09-2017, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T16:33:14-07:00","id":1126876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1126833#post1126833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also feels a little bit... off... that Hunters get Touchstones when regular mortals and even Mages (who are, for the most part, human) do not. That's easily fixed with house rules, though, so it's kind of a non-issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't seem off to me. Hunters rely on networking and cooperation in order to succeed and stay sane. So it fits their themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T19:07:00-07:00","id":1126927,"title":"","content":"I'm interested to see how &quot;Gaining or bestowing power from an obviously monstrous source&quot; is going to interact with Endowments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T19:43:02-07:00","id":1126934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1126876#post1126876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't seem off to me. Hunters rely on networking and cooperation in order to succeed and stay sane. So it fits their themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at it that way, I suppose it <i>does </i>fit. Ah well, something to poke at with a stick if I ever get around to it. I just really like how Touchstones function to keep relationships in the forefront of the game so the characters don't completely drift away and I'm not entirely sure why they aren't in Mage, but that's neither here nor there and has nothing to do with the Code as presented here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1126838#post1126838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters do questionable hard things. Asks a soldier if killing can get easier or harder the more trauma you experience. The assumption is that they become more callous to dealing with the loss of their friends, expecting it to happen again. Also much of the trauma is self inflicted by the things they choose to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I totally get the idea behind the concept, I just find that it rubs me the wrong way a little given how this is a bit of a significant departure from how Integrity is presented elsewhere, especially since almost everything I can recall from just about every sidebar on the subject emphasizes that killing or severely injuring people (or monsters) is preferably always considered a Breaking Point. The only exceptions to that design paradigm I can think of are for Humanity, where you can take a Bane to ignore that particular Breaking Point, and Mage, where you can inure yourself specifically to acts of violence performed with magic. And if you're a Guardian of the Veil with a high Masque Merit, even acts of hubris without magic.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to sound overly negative, I'm just having a hard time understanding how this particular interpretation of Integrity works compared to the standard assumptions of Integrity without being able to see the surrounding text <i>or </i>the associated Breaking Point Conditions. However, the things that are there that I like I really, enthusiastically, appreciate, such as opening up to another character giving you a bonus to Breaking Point rolls and opening up being a necessary prerequisite to regaining Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 08-09-2017, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T23:17:38-07:00","id":1126995,"title":"","content":"It seems a little aggressively one size fits all to me, to be honest. A strong point of baseline Integrity is how much it customizes to the individual character, and a strong point of the old version of the Code was how personal it became. This seems much narrower. Hoping there's more to it. &quot;One statement&quot; doesn't seem like much personal perspective compared to a big required list.<br /> <br /> I like the sound of the Vigilant/ Merciless/Vendetta et al. There's cool bits here. But I came out of that blog with an uncertain feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","user":"Nicias","date":". 08-10-2017, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:58:17-07:00","id":1127050,"title":"","content":"Looks pretty interesting and fun for the most part, except the Exceptional Success on Breaking Point Roll. As far as I know, no other meter punishes players for SUCCEEDING, and seeing how Persistent Obsession hasn't been fan favourite in any of my campaigns, I count that result as punishment. I'm not fan of purchasing points of Morality Meter either, and far prefer the approach of Werewolf and Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T05:47:14-07:00","id":1127070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1126995#post1126995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems a little aggressively one size fits all to me, to be honest. A strong point of baseline Integrity is how much it customizes to the individual character, and a strong point of the old version of the Code was how personal it became. This seems much narrower. Hoping there's more to it. &quot;One statement&quot; doesn't seem like much personal perspective compared to a big required list.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have no plans to approach The Code from a one-size-fits-all angle. Per the text, each player will have the ability to tap into their personal take of the Code, and that may conflict with what their cell, compact, or conspiracy wants to do. How a player defines The Code is what shapes how the rules affect their hunter.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:35:58-07:00","id":1127108,"title":"","content":"Kinda odd that it's still called Integrity when it functions completely differently from the trait non-Hunter humans use. I much preferred how the Code in 1e modified a Hunter's Morality instead of completely replacing the system like this does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:47:24-07:00","id":1127114,"title":"","content":"amm the mechanics themselves seem interesting and appropriate (I love the concept of hunters having Touchstones), but it does strike me a little weird that Hunter's Integrity works different than the regular trait. I'm also not really sure about how the Code works in the new Edition- in the old edition, it was the hunter's ability to modify their psych and accept acts they couldn't accept earlier. When looking at the post, I'm not sure if the Code Breaking Points are example Breaking Points, or that all hunters have the same Code, and only interpret it differently. Having a personal Code is something cool, having one Code for all is a bit stretch- it makes being an hunter into some sort of unified phenomena, as if everyone who hunts monsters thinks in the same way, and that there is one right way to do the Vigil. That feels a bit unrealistic, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:27:43-07:00","id":1127137,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of ideas here that I do like - the Conditions, though we don't know what they all do yet, sound cool, and the Exceptional Success results in particular have interesting implications. I like the idea that events that would traumatize ordinary humans are only traumatic for Hunters until they acclimate or desensitize themselves to them. I like the idea of violating the Code being as damaging to a Hunter's sense of self as an Integrity Breaking Point. I just don't like replacing the Integrity system with this one outright. I prefer it to be a gradual process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:48:39-07:00","id":1127149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127137#post1127137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot of ideas here that I do like - the Conditions, though we don't know what they all do yet, sound cool, and the Exceptional Success results in particular have interesting implications. I like the idea that events that would traumatize ordinary humans are only traumatic for Hunters until they acclimate or desensitize themselves to them. I like the idea of violating the Code being as damaging to a Hunter's sense of self as an Integrity Breaking Point. I just don't like replacing the Integrity system with this one outright. I prefer it to be a gradual process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank-you, you just articulated what I was having trouble placing my finger on. One thing that I love about the CofD's post-human splats (IE. Vampire, Mage, Werewolf, etc.) is how well they emphasize this slow drifting away from humanity, where you can look back on a character's story arc and go &quot;how the hell did we get here?&quot;<br /> <br /> Integrity, for me as a player and a Storyteller, fulfills a similar but different narrative role where it best represents the character's drive and connection to others. If you fight to maintain Integrity, the character can push on, they can endure, but the more Integrity fades away, the more dangerous subsequent encounters with the supernatural become, until it just becomes prudent (and safer) for the character to retire... unless they are willing to risk losing themselves. Obviously, this doesn't work for Hunters, so the Code needs to give them more &quot;staying power&quot;, it needs to push them to react with violence instead of poking their noses into dark corners or keeping their heads down.<br /> <br /> Something I was thinking about last night was, potentially, developing a Code by replacing Integrity Breaking Points with your own Code, lines you won't cross, at the cost of limiting your maximum Integrity. So a Hunter <i>could </i>desensitize themselves to their lifestyle, developing their own lines in the sand, but at the cost of distancing themselves permanently from making a full recovery. Or maybe it would be like a Vampire's Banes instead, penalizing all subsequent Breaking Point rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:01:12-07:00","id":1127153,"title":"","content":"<b>Yeah, I'm all for the Hunters exchanging their own Integrity Breaking Points for other, made from Code, piece by piece.</b> THEN it sounds more like a 1E Code itself. Hunters can start with few - maybe 3-4 - general changed Breaking Points from Integrity, one changed by their Organisation - and each another by their own choosing. <b>And let just call the trait The Code - it's not quite as normal humans Integrity, not enough.</b> <b>Developing Code ( as trait ) could even be marking point between Tier 1 and Tier 2 hunters</b> - Tier 1 are mostly humans and field experience or Organisation did not changed their Integrity enough. Tier 2 are those that respond not quite like rest of humanity then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:15:10-07:00","id":1127160,"title":"","content":"I just want to note that I do like the concept of Cells/Compacts/Conspiracies having each their own Code, which may contrast with the hunter's- that the exact interpretation of the Code and how it differs from hunter to hunter is something interesting to explore. But it also needs to be something which adapts and changes with time- not only the interpretation, but the spirit of the Code itself. Something like that when you become a part of a Cell, you and your cell-mates make together a list which represent you own &quot;Code&quot;, and each Compact/Conspiracy has a Code of its own. Each hunter needs to take a certain amount of Breaking Points from their Cell's list, and a certain number from their Organization's list (if they have one). As their Integrity is exposed to Breaking Points, they may replace existing/add new Breaking Points to mend their psych and allow them to withhold similar trauma in the future- in exchange for becoming more obsessive with the Vigil. Something like that.<br /> <br /> Now, this is only a preview, and we still don't fully know what exactly Monica has in mind- perhaps it is more or less what I want, perhaps it doesn't. We'll have to wait and see. But I do like how falling in Integrity makes the hunter more obsessive and dedicated to the Vigil, and how the Breaking Points mechanics are handled (with the different Conditions which accompany the role). I also like how recovering Integrity is handled, as it totally gives a reason for a hunter to look in the eye of a monster before it shoots it between the eyes and say &quot;before I kill, you, I want you to know why&quot;. I just want it to feel like a personal vow signed with your organization, friends and yourself instead of an objective truth which tells you you are hunting the &quot;right way&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T10:22:23-07:00","id":1127185,"title":"","content":"It might still be called integrity because it's supposed to still count as integrity for things that care about whether something has integrity, like lunacy or dissonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T10:43:08-07:00","id":1127193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127108#post1127108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda odd that it's still called Integrity when it functions completely differently from the trait non-Hunter humans use. I much preferred how the Code in 1e modified a Hunter's Morality instead of completely replacing the system like this does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with the naming convention. It means they're still affected by stuff that deals with Integrity like other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-10-2017, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T10:51:24-07:00","id":1127197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127149#post1127149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank-you, you just articulated what I was having trouble placing my finger on. One thing that I love about the CofD's post-human splats (IE. Vampire, Mage, Werewolf, etc.) is how well they emphasize this slow drifting away from humanity, where you can look back on a character's story arc and go &quot;how the hell did we get here?&quot;<br /> <br /> Integrity, for me as a player and a Storyteller, fulfills a similar but different narrative role where it best represents the character's drive and connection to others. If you fight to maintain Integrity, the character can push on, they can endure, but the more Integrity fades away, the more dangerous subsequent encounters with the supernatural become, until it just becomes prudent (and safer) for the character to retire... unless they are willing to risk losing themselves. Obviously, this doesn't work for Hunters, so the Code needs to give them more &quot;staying power&quot;, it needs to push them to react with violence instead of poking their noses into dark corners or keeping their heads down.<br /> <br /> Something I was thinking about last night was, potentially, developing a Code by replacing Integrity Breaking Points with your own Code, lines you won't cross, at the cost of limiting your maximum Integrity. So a Hunter <i>could </i>desensitize themselves to their lifestyle, developing their own lines in the sand, but at the cost of distancing themselves permanently from making a full recovery. Or maybe it would be like a Vampire's Banes instead, penalizing all subsequent Breaking Point rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I'm thinking I would house-rule The Code if it was published as we see it on this draft.<br /> <br /> The standard Breaking Points for mortals are all &quot;Innate.&quot; Then there could be a few universal Code Breaking Point examples, a few that are particular to certain Compacts and Conspiracies, and players can develop personal Code Breaking Points at ST discretion. The bonuses, penalties, and roll results listed in the preview apply to Code Breaking Points, while Innate Breaking Points follow the normal Integrity rules.<br /> <br /> When you fail an Innate Breaking Point, you can choose to take a Code Breaking Point, linked to your highest available dot of Integrity. If you do so, the failed Innate Breaking Point no longer applies to you. You only roll for Code Breaking Points at or below your current Integrity, but if you have four or more Code Breaking Points associated with dots above your current Integrity you take a -1 penalty to Code Breaking Point rolls and gain the Persistent Vigilant Condition. If you have 7 or more Code Breaking Points associated with dots above your current Integrity, the penalty increases to -2 and you gain the Persistent Merciless Condition. If you have 10 Code Breaking Points above your current Integrity, you become a Slasher.<br /> <br /> I think that's the best way to keep the mechanics as true to the preview as possible while making it a modification to standard Integrity instead of a replacement for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T10:52:20-07:00","id":1127199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127185#post1127185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might still be called integrity because it's supposed to still count as integrity for things that care about whether something has integrity, like lunacy or dissonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T10:54:42-07:00","id":1127200,"title":"","content":"One reason to keep the name would be because hunters are just regular people who've taken up an extraordinary task. The rules have changed to reflect how the vigil changes the hunter, but the intent and usage hasn't. In fact, with this precedent it's quite possible that other Breaking Point inducing occupations such as deployed military, police officers in certain countries, gang members, and cults that have successfully made supernatural contact. The only reason we don't have specific Integrity rules for them would be because we don't have gamelines about them (although I'd really like to see a 2E blue book about cultists that does explore how their Integrity is changed by their specific experiences).<br /> <br /> Another reason to change the rules would be to give hunters more of an identity separate from regular people. Especially since there's a myriad of Supernatural Merits available for regular people in 2E that balances the Endowments available to some hunters. Having an updated Integrity system helps justify hunters having a gameline rather than being a collection of themed blue books.<br /> <br /> Edit: And three new posts was written before I finished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:07:37-07:00","id":1127234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127200#post1127200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another reason to change the rules would be to give hunters more of an identity separate from regular people. Especially since there's a myriad of Supernatural Merits available for regular people in 2E that balances the Endowments available to some hunters. Having an updated Integrity system helps justify hunters having a gameline rather than being a collection of themed blue books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is actually exactly why I'm not a fan of completely replacing the system for Integrity. Part of the appeal of Vigil to me is that anyone could become a Hunter. It's just a matter of experiencing the supernatural and deciding to do something about it instead of falling into the CofD human tendency to deny it. I like them having cool exceptions to the normal human rules, but I like them to layer on top of the normal human rules instead of replacing them to further blur the lines between human, Hunter, and Slasher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:37:49-07:00","id":1127245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127200#post1127200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One reason to keep the name would be because hunters are just regular people who've taken up an extraordinary task. The rules have changed to reflect how the vigil changes the hunter, but the intent and usage hasn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're spot-on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:48:22-07:00","id":1127251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127070#post1127070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have no plans to approach The Code from a one-size-fits-all angle. Per the text, each player will have the ability to tap into their personal take of the Code, and that may conflict with what their cell, compact, or conspiracy wants to do. How a player defines The Code is what shapes how the rules affect their hunter.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Looking forward to seeing how that works!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:35:59-07:00","id":1127292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127234#post1127234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is actually exactly why I'm not a fan of completely replacing the system for Integrity. Part of the appeal of Vigil to me is that anyone could become a Hunter. It's just a matter of experiencing the supernatural and deciding to do something about it instead of falling into the CofD human tendency to deny it. I like them having cool exceptions to the normal human rules, but I like them to layer on top of the normal human rules instead of replacing them to further blur the lines between human, Hunter, and Slasher.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what to think of it yet. In a way it feels more like an optional rule for the regular core book but that's probably just me not seeing the point of HtV being separate from the blue books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T16:13:26-07:00","id":1127388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazy_Ivan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127050#post1127050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks pretty interesting and fun for the most part, except the Exceptional Success on Breaking Point Roll. As far as I know, no other meter punishes players for SUCCEEDING, and seeing how Persistent Obsession hasn't been fan favourite in any of my campaigns, I count that result as punishment. I'm not fan of purchasing points of Morality Meter either, and far prefer the approach of Werewolf and Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As it is, I don't actually have a problem with that. Addicted may need to kick the bucket, but Obsession makes sense as a Success Condition-the hunter, shaken, rededicates herself to her job to channel the stress positively. After the Obsession is dealt with (ie, the Hunt ends), the hunter realizes she was acting irrationally and takes some time off to de-stress. <br /> <br /> As it is, Hunter Obsession should probably give some nice bonuses to show how determination is really an effective coping mechanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T01:50:28-07:00","id":1127523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127388#post1127388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As it is, I don't actually have a problem with that. Addicted may need to kick the bucket, but Obsession makes sense as a Success Condition-the hunter, shaken, rededicates herself to her job to channel the stress positively. After the Obsession is dealt with (ie, the Hunt ends), the hunter realizes she was acting irrationally and takes some time off to de-stress.<br /> <br /> As it is, Hunter Obsession should probably give some nice bonuses to show how determination is really an effective coping mechanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds better, but I was going off from the information we have, and that is the normal Obsession Condition, which doesn't give much bonuses. It's especially harmful when game isn't laser focused on one monster, and thus most rolls suffer. Also, the Condition being Persistent on Exceptional Success is still counter-intuitive to me; the stronger mind the hunter has, the more likely he becomes mentally scarred, removed from humanity and deeply obsessed?<br /> <br /> Until we see what the Conditions do, I can't say I would use the system as written.<br /> <br /> Edit. I like that realization and de-stress angle you mentioned. I'll propably use houserule that successfully resolving Persisten Conditions gained from breaking points allows to raise Integrity once per story. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","user":"Crazy_Ivan","date":". 08-11-2017, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T15:43:43-07:00","id":1127802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazy_Ivan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1127523#post1127523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit. I like that realization and de-stress angle you mentioned. I'll propably use houserule that successfully resolving Persisten Conditions gained from breaking points allows to raise Integrity once per story. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure this is why all of the Persistent Conditions you can get from a Dramatically Failed Integrity Breaking Point roll can be resolved by gaining a point of Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T08:49:31-07:00","id":1128059,"title":"","content":"I like that, based on the description, the Code should protect against the amnesia effects of the Sleeping Curse. Not the integrity hit, mind, just the amnesia. That's good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T09:34:43-07:00","id":1128073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128059#post1128059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that, based on the description, the Code should protect against the amnesia effects of the Sleeping Curse. Not the integrity hit, mind, just the amnesia. That's good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do you draw that conclusion from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T09:46:33-07:00","id":1128076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128059#post1128059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that, based on the description, the Code should protect against the amnesia effects of the Sleeping Curse. Not the integrity hit, mind, just the amnesia. That's good.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T10:50:45-07:00","id":1128086,"title":"","content":"There's stuff that I like here but there are also a couple of major sticking points that are sort of bothering me. The biggest one is that it puts a lot of focus on hunters as aggressive and violent people who go out and murder monsters, which makes the game feel less like &quot;people who see what everyone else looks away from and take a stand&quot; and more &quot;let's go murder some scary magic things.&quot; I'm really not sure how well it would play in groups that focus more on the less violent sides of The Vigil, like Network Zero's fight against the veil/masquerade or the Barret Commission's work keeping vampires out of politics. Violence might happen along the way, but that's not really what they're about. I've had problems in the past where the majority of my players were on board to do a social/investigative plot but one of them got the impression that hunter was all about the big guns and monster killin' and tried to go around shooting plot hooks, and while that's something that really just needed to be talked out ahead of time at the table I could see passages like this leading to similar problems for people who didn't learn that lesson the hard way.<br /> <br /> The way people come to The Code also feels a bit odd. The way it's written, being something a lot of people come to themselves but also universal in its tenants, it almost reads like there's a magical universal hive mind whose basic moral underpinnings all hunters intuitively understand. If it's something that's usually shared socially as some kind of wider hunter culture and tier one gets lumped into the same mechanics for simplicity I'm fine with that, but it doesn't come off that way here.<br /> <br /> Those aside I really like what I'm seeing. I especially like that a lot of breaking points are only called for the first time something happens, acknowledging that it's a traumatic event but not making day to day hunter business a race to see how quickly you can drop to integrity 3, and I really love that hunters can only regain integrity through an open, honest connection with someone. It strikes a good balance between the active and dedicated humanist perspective that I liked playing to in 1e while keeping the &quot;he who fights monsters should see to it that he does not become a monster&quot; theme in plain view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:07:34-07:00","id":1128091,"title":"","content":"This is a bit of a mixed bag for me.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I love the idea of picking up Persistent conditions as your Integrity drops - that has potential. I also like that they use a different set of Conditions for DF/F/S/ES. I also like the expanded list of penalties - feels pretty appropriate (though &quot;actively and willingly helping a monster&quot; feels a bit off - it's an action, not a modifier). Oh, and the Touchstones/using Touchstones as a prerequisite to gaining Integrity is <i>pretty great</i>.<br /> <br /> On the <i>other</i> hand... I hate the scale. The one thing that made mortal Integrity interesting to me is that Breaking Points are <i>negotiable</i>. Nothing is, strictly speaking, innate - there's a step where you can suggest that, hey, this wouldn't count as a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> Like, I dunno... I kinda want to see this as a &quot;template&quot; you slap over mortal Integrity. Something like this, maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Code acts like a second Virtue for the purposes of Breaking Points - it always is appropriate when going after monsters, and different Hunter groups have their own tweaks to when you can use it. Additionally, you can add &quot;rules&quot; to your personal Code - they supply additional bonuses when The Code applies, and widen what qualifies as &quot;violating&quot; The Code. Dot your i's and cross your t's, and you'll be safe and secure.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can lean on The Code in a more hardcore way - you can use it to just plain say &quot;no&quot; to rolling whenever it would apply. Whenever you do this, you have to take an appropriate condition, which can only be resolved by opening up to a Touchstone. Opening up to a Touchstone is also required to buy up Integrity, so you should do it consistently.<br /> <br /> Oh and by the way, <i>violating The Code is, itself, a Breaking Point</i>. Just thought you should know. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T11:38:23-07:00","id":1128106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128076#post1128076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>So now we have a confirmed, &quot;the Code doesn't keep you from suffering the Sleeper's Curse.&quot; I'm assuming that means it also doesn't make you immune to Lunacy or Disquiet either. Does the Code provide a chance roll to resist Lunacy or Disquiet? I'm curious (was curious back in 1e too) how Hunters without innate abilities (Endowments like Castigations, Supernatural merits) can remember the supernatural forces or creatures they've hunted or are hunting. Innate supernatural abilities, be they merits or endowments does make a person a Sleepwalker by definition if memory serves right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T12:34:22-07:00","id":1128124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128086#post1128086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those aside I really like what I'm seeing. I especially like that a lot of breaking points are only called for the first time something happens, acknowledging that it's a traumatic event but not making day to day hunter business a race to see how quickly you can drop to integrity 3, and I really love that hunters can only regain integrity through an open, honest connection with someone. It strikes a good balance between the active and dedicated humanist perspective that I liked playing to in 1e while keeping the &quot;he who fights monsters should see to it that he does not become a monster&quot; theme in plain view.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>For me better balance would be next killing monster to move on 'Integrity Tier' higher, not miss it totally in Code</b> - most of the time it would not make difference - first time killing monster in Integrity 4-6, so next monster killings would be on Integrity 7-10 - i.e. most character once killing particular monster would not be moved by killing another. BUT if character would strife to high Integrity ( like 9-10 ) it would become more and more problem for her - and <b>highlight that Vigil, in the end, is self-destructive obsession for mortal, nothing truly 'healthy' for character.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-12-2017, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T12:49:09-07:00","id":1128129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128124#post1128124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>For me better balance would be next killing monster to move on 'Integrity Tier' higher, not miss it totally in Code</b> - most of the time it would not make difference - first time killing monster in Integrity 4-6, so next monster killings would be on Integrity 7-10 - i.e. most character once killing particular monster would not be moved by killing another. <b>BUT <i>if</i> character would strife to high Integrity ( like 9-10 ) it would become more and more problem for her - and highlight that Vigil, in the end, is self-destructive obsession for mortal, nothing truly 'healthy' for character.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If you bold every second sentence in your post, it makes it impossible to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T12:56:25-07:00","id":1128130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128106#post1128106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now we have a confirmed, &quot;the Code doesn't keep you from suffering the Sleeper's Curse.&quot; I'm assuming that means it also doesn't make you immune to Lunacy or Disquiet either. Does the Code provide a chance roll to resist Lunacy or Disquiet? I'm curious (was curious back in 1e too) how Hunters without innate abilities (Endowments like Castigations, Supernatural merits) can remember the supernatural forces or creatures they've hunted or are hunting. Innate supernatural abilities, be they merits or endowments does make a person a Sleepwalker by definition if memory serves right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, I would really rather not have this argument again. I think it's time we all just accept that, by default setting assumptions, Hunters without innate supernatural abilities or the Sleepwalker Merit have no way of circumventing these sorts of memory altering effects, and if you want there to be a way, you can house rule it. I'm a supporter of hunters having ways to cope with such effects, but it's just not. worth. fighting over any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:02:27-07:00","id":1128136,"title":"","content":"Lunacy shouldn't be too much of an issue. It doesn't always force a memory loss, and people working together, like a cell, or who have been injured by a werewolf, get bonuses to it. It's still a fearful experience but, again, doesn't always make people forget what happened.<br /> <br /> Mage has a 1-dot Merit to make you a Sleepwalker and turn you immune to the Curse and cause no Dissonance.<br /> <br /> As Charlaquin has implied, this was confirmed long ago. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages\">Here's a link</a> to one of the primary threads about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-12-2017, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T13:13:50-07:00","id":1128146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128086#post1128086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's stuff that I like here but there are also a couple of major sticking points that are sort of bothering me. The biggest one is that it puts a lot of focus on hunters as aggressive and violent people who go out and murder monsters, which makes the game feel less like &amp;quot;people who see what everyone else looks away from and take a stand&amp;quot; and more &amp;quot;let's go murder some scary magic things.&amp;quot; I'm really not sure how well it would play in groups that focus more on the less violent sides of The Vigil, like Network Zero's fight against the veil/masquerade or the Barret Commission's work keeping vampires out of politics. Violence might happen along the way, but that's not really what they're about. I've had problems in the past where the majority of my players were on board to do a social/investigative plot but one of them got the impression that hunter was all about the big guns and monster killin' and tried to go around shooting plot hooks, and while that's something that really just needed to be talked out ahead of time at the table I could see passages like this leading to similar problems for people who didn't learn that lesson the hard way.<br /> <br /> The way people come to The Code also feels a bit odd. The way it's written, being something a lot of people come to themselves but also universal in its tenants, it almost reads like there's a magical universal hive mind whose basic moral underpinnings all hunters intuitively understand. If it's something that's usually shared socially as some kind of wider hunter culture and tier one gets lumped into the same mechanics for simplicity I'm fine with that, but it doesn't come off that way here.<br /> <br /> Those aside I really like what I'm seeing. I especially like that a lot of breaking points are only called for the first time something happens, acknowledging that it's a traumatic event but not making day to day hunter business a race to see how quickly you can drop to integrity 3, and I really love that hunters can only regain integrity through an open, honest connection with someone. It strikes a good balance between the active and dedicated humanist perspective that I liked playing to in 1e while keeping the &amp;quot;he who fights monsters should see to it that he does not become a monster&amp;quot; theme in plain view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out Hurt Locker. Not all violence is physical or a life or death matter. Violence is about dominance. Power.<br /> <br /> I agree with the notions about the innate Code breaches being arbitrary running counter to the spirit of Integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:58:53-07:00","id":1128208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128076#post1128076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's bad.<br /> <br /> My read was that the Code is about hardening the mind against the supernatural, and Mage 2E explicitly states the amnesia is a consequence of the human mind protecting itself - the Code is a clear mechanism for providing an alternative hardening, then.<br /> <br /> But I actually did not like how Mage 2E handled sleepwalkers (especially compared to how Werewolf 2E handled Lunacy) and it's clear the design attitude disagrees with me, so, whatever, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 08-12-2017, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T15:21:14-07:00","id":1128220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128208#post1128208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's bad.<br /> <br /> My read was that the Code is about hardening the mind against the supernatural, and Mage 2E explicitly states the amnesia is a consequence of the human mind protecting itself - the Code is a clear mechanism for providing an alternative hardening, then.<br /> <br /> But I actually did not like how Mage 2E handled sleepwalkers (especially compared to how Werewolf 2E handled Lunacy) and it's clear the design attitude disagrees with me, so, whatever, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt Dave's gonna send ninjas to your home if you decide the Code equals a 1 dot merit which you'd give to your players for free and thus wouldn't need to write down in their sheet to begin with. Golden rule and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T15:27:06-07:00","id":1128223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128220#post1128220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt Dave's gonna send ninjas to your home if you decide the Code equals a 1 dot merit which you'd give to your players for free and thus wouldn't need to write down in their sheet to begin with. Golden rule and all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd rather not have to be house-ruling in the first place? It's a 1 dot merit that won't appear in Hunter itself, a 1 dot merit tax that isn't necessary to support either the themes of Hunter or Mage, and I think the attitude behind how Sleepwalkers are handled is actively toxic to Mage itself as a gameline (and obviously bad for crossover purposes with Hunter) and not reflective of how the nWoD second editions have improved in design overall. When Lunacy went from binary to dynamic, the Sleeping Curse went from binary to more binary. It's weird and annoys me.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I can just golden rule it, but you asked. I'll drop the subject though if it's been discussed ad nauseum already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 08-12-2017, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T16:04:00-07:00","id":1128237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128146#post1128146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Check out Hurt Locker. Not all violence is physical or a life or death matter. Violence is about dominance. Power.<br /> <br /> I agree with the notions about the innate Code breaches being arbitrary running counter to the spirit of Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue isn't that the idea of violence is there, it's that within the context of hunter (or at least this section) it's about blood or savagery or the person behind the flamethrower. There's a couple of mentions toward how a hunter might be more manipulative in the same way they could be violent, but it's easy to gloss over.<br /> <br /> Generally I'd like to see as much as possible that the game is more about hunters as the people who see the big nasty magic stuff and deal with it when others can't or won't, rather than the guys that grab guns and flamethrowers to murder scary things. The mechanics of this mostly do an alright job of that, it just doesn't feel that way when you read the flavor and background around it.<br /> <br /> I'll also say that at least for my part I don't mind the fixed breaking points used here. It's more flexible and customizable than most integrity equivalents, and I prefer it to the system in 1e where you kept your sanity by acting more psychologically damaged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T16:44:57-07:00","id":1128252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128223#post1128223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd rather not have to be house-ruling in the first place? It's a 1 dot merit that won't appear in Hunter itself, a 1 dot merit tax that isn't necessary to support either the themes of Hunter or Mage, and I think the attitude behind how Sleepwalkers are handled is actively toxic to Mage itself as a gameline (and obviously bad for crossover purposes with Hunter) and not reflective of how the nWoD second editions have improved in design overall. When Lunacy went from binary to dynamic, the Sleeping Curse went from binary to more binary. It's weird and annoys me.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I can just golden rule it, but you asked. I'll drop the subject though if it's been discussed ad nauseum already.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't read me. No need to tax any PC. Just regard all Hunters with any sufficient exposure to the supernal as sleepwalkers without wasting sheet space for a 1 dot merit if that's how you want to run the game.<br /> <br /> There aren't perfect games. Specially if you rely on third parties to deliver things to your exact expectations while you aren't the guy in charge for it. *shrug*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T16:49:17-07:00","id":1128254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128237#post1128237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue isn't that the idea of violence is there, it's that within the context of hunter (or at least this section) it's about blood or savagery or the person behind the flamethrower. There's a couple of mentions toward how a hunter might be more manipulative in the same way they could be violent, but it's easy to gloss over.<br /> <br /> Generally I'd like to see as much as possible that the game is more about hunters as the people who see the big nasty magic stuff and deal with it when others can't or won't, rather than the guys that grab guns and flamethrowers to murder scary things. The mechanics of this mostly do an alright job of that, it just doesn't feel that way when you read the flavor and background around it.<br /> <br /> I'll also say that at least for my part I don't mind the fixed breaking points used here. It's more flexible and customizable than most integrity equivalents, and I prefer it to the system in 1e where you kept your sanity by acting more psychologically damaged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Picking up a flame-thrower and trying to roast the thing that terrifies you whilst trying to maintain the lid on growing paranoid thoughts barely contained by a thin connection with someone you know wouldn't have to suffer such fate sounds as human as it gets; IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T12:46:06-07:00","id":1128552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128254#post1128254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Picking up a flame-thrower and trying to roast the thing that terrifies you whilst trying to maintain the lid on growing paranoid thoughts barely contained by a thin connection with someone you know wouldn't have to suffer such fate sounds as human as it gets; IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's all fine, I'd just like to see the game take a broader focus on how and why people take a stand against the things that go bump in the night. Making the game just about the visceral parts or the psychological damage is fine if that's what you or your group want, but there are a lot of other creepy or compelling stories you can tell with hunters of other stripes. For me, at least, the game is less interesting if it leans toward lumping most hunters into the &quot;integrity 6 or lower killing machine&quot; box.<br /> <br /> I get the sense that what I'm looking for is in the drafts they're doing already on some level, I just wanted to give my two cents since this draft brought it to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T13:05:29-07:00","id":1128559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128552#post1128552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's all fine, I'd just like to see the game take a broader focus on how and why people take a stand against the things that go bump in the night. Making the game just about the visceral parts or the psychological damage is fine if that's what you or your group want, but there are a lot of other creepy or compelling stories you can tell with hunters of other stripes. For me, at least, the game is less interesting if it leans toward lumping most hunters into the &amp;quot;integrity 6 or lower killing machine&amp;quot; box.<br /> <br /> I get the sense that what I'm looking for is in the drafts they're doing already on some level, I just wanted to give my two cents since this draft brought it to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have better luck if you define your &quot;broader strokes&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:34:33-07:00","id":1128593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1126808-open-dev-the-code?p=1128552#post1128552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's all fine, I'd just like to see the game take a broader focus on how and why people take a stand against the things that go bump in the night. Making the game just about the visceral parts or the psychological damage is fine if that's what you or your group want, but there are a lot of other creepy or compelling stories you can tell with hunters of other stripes. For me, at least, the game is less interesting if it leans toward lumping most hunters into the &quot;integrity 6 or lower killing machine&quot; box.</div> </div> </div> </div>They really don't seem to be going towards depicting all hunters as killing machines, especially with the emphasis on actual killing machines as an antagonist.<br /> <br /> That said, a hunter isn't just someone who has a ghost in their house and deals with it then moves on with their life. Hunters have been fundamentally changed, not just by their experience, but by the decision to change their life, devoting themselves to doing something about it, not just when it effects them. Even one who abstains from killing is going to be encountering mind-breaking things that will hit their Integrity. Most Breaking Points aren't the result of something the character does as much as something the character has seen, or something that's been done to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-13-2017, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}